host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan enlist -- a phase may join a run already under way, and the run's memory is what keeps the order honest
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, deep-read one council-rota doc, send the increment.
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md end to end -- rows 80 and 84 through 87 all carry closures, #85's reopening on 20260819.134229 closed with the witness_claim_check loom on metal, and #84's late closure note landed 20260819.145920. No open agent-closable red, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came from the newest log's own recommend rather than from REMEMBER alone -- arrive.rye had just closed and named its successor exactly: an arrival is answered at the door, before the run begins, so a supervisor with children already in flight still had no way to take work.
think Council rota by lap index -- 477 .kyri logs on disk when the lap opened, so this is lap 478, and 478 mod 27 = 19, which is context/KYRI.md. Read it first, ahead of REMEMBER, so the voice shaped the reasoning from the first token. Its line "measurement beats memory -- when a first look and a second look disagree, the second look wins, in public" is what this round then had to live out, twice over.
think The first reading was wrong, and the RED said so on the first run. The design had a new refusal in it -- TurnSpent, for a newcomer whose turn some already-started phase follows -- and the happy-zone check reddened at "the door-time reading refused the late phase on its own." The reason is exact: arrive.rye's awaited test reads every phase in the plan, taken or waiting, so spent implies awaited and the new refusal was strictly weaker than the one already there. Dead code, caught before it shipped.
think The correction is the better finding. The mid-run door needs no new name at all; it needs a memory. The three facts arrive.rye reads are facts about the phases a run was EVER handed, so read against the whole record they mean at the tenth child exactly what they meant before the first -- and the honest new claim is what a run must never do, which is forget what it spent.
think The forgetting is measurable rather than assertable, so the module measures it. The same phase is refused by name against a record of 6 and welcomed back by the very same reading over the 4 still waiting -- a supervisor keeping only remaining work would run a phase a second time, behind its own follower, with out_of_precede reading zero the whole way.
think The supervisor loop is restated here rather than delegated, which is this arc's idiom: arrange delegated because it added nothing to the loop, precede restated because it added a counter. This rung restates because the record's length is a running fact rather than a constant read from the plan it was handed -- held, not plan.len, is what makes the table different from every elder one.
think Naming, under the Comlink tendency. join was taken by the Lotus audio family, late reads as a judgment rather than a fact, and admit is already a verb across four caravan rungs -- so enlist was drawn: plain, warm, and free everywhere in the tree.
obs The passes differ honestly and the honesty is the point: 1 handed whole against 0 joined while running. Work that has not arrived yet is work a blocked head cannot pass over, so the growing run reaches less and still lands 7 children at the same end with 0 named turns broken. A rung that had forced the two numbers to match would have been hiding a real difference.
obs The bounds turned out simpler than the design guessed. max_enlist_tests was written as twice the arrival cost while the second walk existed; with the walk gone it is exactly max_arrival_tests, and the comptime invariant now states the equality rather than an inequality -- joining late costs precisely what arriving at the door costs.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim. Weigh the newcomer against the work still waiting rather than the record and the pure read reds at a phase the run already spent joining a second time; wave every newcomer through and it reds the same way -- so the single refusal is load-bearing rather than decorative, and the remainder view exists only to price the forgetting.
obs Thirty-seven green-witnessed Rye rings now carry the Microkit shape across real processes. TAME surface GREEN -- style bans clean, width-check exit 0 -- and the neighbor rung re-GREEN: caravan_arrive_witness passed unchanged beside the new one.
obs The limit is named rather than implied, in the module banner, the README, and the witness header alike: a newcomer joins the tail and waits its turn, never preempting a child already running. Whether a run may withdraw a phase still waiting is the mirror of this rung and belongs to the vision room until a witness binds it.
loom witness=caravan_enlist_witness enlist_tests_max=16 seating_tests_max=256 record_len=6 remaining_len=4 newcomers=3 children=7 passes_whole=1 passes_growing=0 turns_broken=0
file caravan/enlist.rye the rung -- a record that grows while it runs, one walk per enlistment, and the remainder view that prices what forgetting costs
file tools/caravan_enlist_witness.rish the witness on metal -- native contains checks, both RED paths recorded in the header
file caravan/README.md the durable Enlist section, placed after Arrive and before Held, carrying the numbers and the named limit
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moved to this rung; the arrive edge folded into the prior-edges pointer
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back cairn recorded before the card was condensed, at nib 45ae32e474
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is the mirror this rung named -- a phase may now join a run under way, and nothing may yet leave one; the question becomes whether a run may withdraw a phase still waiting without stranding a phase that named its turn, which wants a lap reading what a withdrawal owes the plan the way an arrival owed it three facts.
